   ```java
   throw new IllegalArgumentException(
       "GSON (" + GsonBuildConfig.VERSION + ") cannot handle " + type);
   ```

6. For the outermost adapter request, it publishes all adapters resolved during that request into the shared cache:

   ```java
   typeTokenCache.putAll(threadCalls);
   ```

How it avoids infinite recursion for self-referential / cyclic types:

- During resolution, before the real adapter exists, `getAdapter` stores a `FutureTypeAdapter` placeholder in the thread-local `threadCalls` map.
- If resolving the same type recursively reaches `getAdapter` again, this code detects the in-progress adapter:

  ```java
  TypeAdapter<T> ongoingCall = (TypeAdapter<T>) threadCalls.get(type);
  if (ongoingCall != null) {
    return ongoingCall;
  }
